cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or build on this work, please cite the paper below."
title: "Drift-Resilient Indoor 3D Mapping in GPS-Denied Environments Using RKO-LIO with Velodyne–Pixhawk Integration in ROS 2"
abstract: >-
  Indoor 3D mapping system integrating a Velodyne VLP-16 LiDAR and a Pixhawk Cube
  Orange+ IMU on a TurtleBot Waffle Pi running ROS 2 Humble, evaluating RKO-LIO
  (a sensor-agnostic LiDAR–inertial odometry method) against LIO-SAM and FAST-LIO.
  Real-robot validation achieves centimeter-level accuracy (RMSE 0.026 m), and a
  controlled Gazebo simulation benchmark exposes the accuracy–robustness trade-off
  across three GPS-denied indoor environments.
type: software
